<ltml units="in" margin="0.5">
  <font id="body" name="Helvetica" size="12" />
  <pagestyle id="compact" width="6in" height="5.5in" />
  <bullet id="brand-star" shape="star" width="24pt" r="5pt" brush="Gold" pen="solid" points="5" r0="2.5pt" />
  <bullet id="ordered-mark" font="body" />
  <page style="compact" font="body" layout="vbox" layout.vpadding="8pt">
    <div display="always" align="top" border="dashed" padding="5pt" width="100%">
      <label display="always" font.weight="Bold">List splitting</label>
      <label display="always">Ordered lists should continue numbering across pages.</label>
    </div>

    <vbox border="dotted" padding="5pt" layout.vpadding="4pt" width="100%">
      <label font.weight="Bold">Default unordered list</label>
      <ul>
        <p>Default unordered list items use a built-in disc marker.</p>
        <p>Only direct child paragraphs receive markers automatically.</p>
      </ul>

      <label font.weight="Bold">Default ordered list</label>
      <ol>
        <p>Default ordered list items use decimal markers.</p>
        <p>Markers auto-size so double-digit ordinals stay aligned.</p>
      </ol>

      <label font.weight="Bold">Custom bullets</label>
      <ul bullets="brand-star">
        <p>Custom unordered lists can reuse named bullet styles.</p>
        <p>This example uses a filled star marker.</p>
      </ul>
    </vbox>

    <ol bullets="ordered-mark" border="solid" padding="8pt" layout.vpadding="6pt">
      <p>
        This first ordered item is intentionally long so the list container must
        split it across pages without reprinting the marker on the continuation
        fragment. Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do
        eiusmod tempor incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim
        veniam, quis nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea
        commodo consequat. Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit
        esse cillum dolore eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat
        non proident, sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.
        Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit, sed do eiusmod tempor
        incididunt ut labore et dolore magna aliqua. Ut enim ad minim veniam, quis
        nostrud exercitation ullamco laboris nisi ut aliquip ex ea commodo consequat.
        Duis aute irure dolor in reprehenderit in voluptate velit esse cillum dolore
        eu fugiat nulla pariatur. Excepteur sint occaecat cupidatat non proident,
        sunt in culpa qui officia deserunt mollit anim id est laborum.
      </p>
      <p>Second ordered item continues the numbering after the split.</p>
      <p>Third ordered item confirms numbering remains stable on later fragments.</p>
      <p>Fourth ordered item keeps the decimal sequence going.</p>
      <p>Fifth ordered item leaves enough content to require a continuation page.</p>
      <p>Sixth ordered item should not restart at one.</p>
      <p>Seventh ordered item remains aligned with the rest of the list.</p>
      <p>Eighth ordered item gives the second page more than one ordinal.</p>
      <p>Ninth ordered item keeps the list moving.</p>
      <p>Tenth ordered item exercises double-digit width alignment.</p>
      <p>Eleventh ordered item keeps the auto-sized marker slot in use.</p>
      <p>Twelfth ordered item closes the sample.</p>
      <p>Thirteenth ordered item keeps the list going.</p>
      <p>Fourteenth ordered item adds one more body row.</p>
      <p>Fifteenth ordered item confirms numbering stays monotonic.</p>
      <p>Sixteenth ordered item leaves no room for a restart bug.</p>
      <p>Seventeenth ordered item ensures a later fragment still has markers.</p>
      <p>Eighteenth ordered item keeps the footer and marker logic busy.</p>
      <p>Nineteenth ordered item remains aligned in the same slot width.</p>
      <p>Twentieth ordered item finishes the ordered sequence.</p>
    </ol>

    <div display="always" align="bottom" border="dotted" padding="3pt" margin-top="4pt" width="100%">
      <label display="odd">Odd list footer</label>
      <label display="even">Even list footer</label>
    </div>
  </page>
</ltml>
